437
00:16:54,611 --> 00:16:56,577
Those that are using it more than that,

438
00:16:56,577 --> 00:16:57,750
there's ways of knowing

439
00:16:57,750 --> 00:16:59,100
that they're using it more than that,

440
00:16:59,100 --> 00:16:59,933
and it's reflecting.

441
00:16:59,933 --> 00:17:02,550
People are like, "Oh, I think just stuck it in Copilot,"

442
00:17:02,550 --> 00:17:03,750
you know, in that way.

443
00:17:03,750 --> 00:17:05,314
Does that help?

444
00:17:05,314 --> 00:17:08,790
- I'll add from my perspective at Jobs for the Future,

445
00:17:08,790 --> 00:17:11,820
I've been, I've sort of switched my philosophy

446
00:17:11,820 --> 00:17:12,930
where I used to start off

447
00:17:12,930 --> 00:17:15,720
with having different AI tools like Copilot

448
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:18,630
or ChatGPT create a first draft.

449
00:17:18,630 --> 00:17:21,660
And I was realizing I was getting a lot of gobblygook

450
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:23,100
that didn't make a lot of sense.

451
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:25,200
So I've started off with drafting something myself

452
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:27,127
and then giving really specific commands of,

453
00:17:27,127 --> 00:17:29,580
"Make it more persuasive, make it more pithy,

454
00:17:29,580 --> 00:17:31,290
make it for a C-level executive,

455
00:17:31,290 --> 00:17:32,640
put it in this voice."

456
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:34,780
- I asked it to make it non-AI the other day

457
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:36,000
after it being persuasive.

458
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,309
I said, "Now make it more human," or, "less AI."

459
00:17:38,309 --> 00:17:40,276
It was amazing. It did it.

460
00:17:40,276 --> 00:17:41,790
And I was like, "Okay, that sounds more like me.

461
00:17:41,790 --> 00:17:44,100
You've taken it back from here to here."

462
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:45,960
But it's almost not being afraid.

463
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:47,466
Yeah, but I'm the same.

464
00:17:47,466 --> 00:17:48,994
I don't write the first draft in it.

465
00:17:48,994 --> 00:17:50,340
Yeah, it's the fine, fine-tuning.

466
00:17:50,340 --> 00:17:52,232
- Yeah, that's exactly it.

